.TH HOMELAB-CLI-ADMIN 8 "2026-08-21" "homelab-cli" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
homelab-cli\-admin \- site administration commands for homelab\-cli
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homelab-cli
.RB [ --api-url
.IR url ]
.B admin
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B homelab-cli admin
groups user- and role-management operations under one command family:
.B user
and
.BR role .
Every action requires the logged-in account to hold the
.I site_admin
role server-side; the CLI does not enforce this locally, the server
does.
.P
Each of
.B user
and
.B role
takes exactly one action flag per invocation (they're mutually
exclusive), plus whatever flags that action needs. Run
.RI "\(lqhomelab-cli admin " command " --help\(rq"
for the full flag list.
.SH "USER ACTIONS"
.RI "(\(lqhomelab-cli admin user " "--flag ..." "\(rq)"
.TP
.B --create
Create a dovecot.users account (idempotent) and assign it an initial
role. Requires
.BR --email " and " --role .
Generates a random server-side password and prints it once \- never
accepts a client-supplied password. If the account already exists, no
password is generated; the role is still (idempotently) assigned.
.TP
.B --list
List all accounts, their roles, and active flag.
.TP
.B --list-roles
List
.BR --email 's
roles.
.TP
.BI --add-role " ROLE"
Assign
.I ROLE
to
.BR --email .
.TP
.BI --remove-role " ROLE"
Revoke
.I ROLE
from
.BR --email .
.TP
.B --reset-password
Reset
.BR --email 's
password to a randomly generated dictionary passphrase, printed once.
Not recoverable afterward; if lost, reset again.
.TP
.BR --revoke-all-tokens ", " --force-relogin
Revoke all of
.BR --email 's
refresh tokens, forcing re-login on their next token refresh. Both
flags perform the identical action against two distinct server
endpoints of the same name \- pick whichever name reads better in
context.
.SH "ROLE ACTIONS"
.RI "(\(lqhomelab-cli admin role " "--flag ..." "\(rq)"
.TP
.B --create
Create a new role (idempotent). Requires
.BR --role ,
optionally
.BR --description .
.TP
.B --remove-role
Delete
.BR --role .
Refused if it's
.IR site_admin " or " user ,
or if any user still holds it.
.TP
.B --list
List all roles, each with its granted endpoint permissions.
.TP
.B --add-permissions
Grant one or more endpoints to
.B --role
(via
.BR --permissions ,
e.g.
.RI \(lqGET\ /api/v1/drive/quota\(rq ).
Endpoints already on the role are left as-is.
.TP
.B --remove-permissions
Revoke one or more endpoints from
.B --role
(via
.BR --permissions ).
Endpoints not on the role are left as-is.
.TP
.B --list-all-available-role-permissions
List every endpoint that could be granted to a role.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR homelab-cli (8),
.BR homelab-cli-mail (8),
.BR homelab-cli-drive (8)
